\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 EFE International's Topics of the Day for July 31, 2023 (20.00 GMT)\b0\par\par\uc2 1,443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE WAR\par \par \uc2 Moscow/Kiev - Ukraine and Russia intensify fighting along the entire frontline, from the south of the country to the heart of the Donbas, amid growing international demands for a ceasefire and the convening of a meeting to stop the war in Saudi Arabia without the presence of the Kremlin. (Text) (Photo) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 Kiev - Ukraine today confirmed the start of talks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Saudi Arabia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of international representatives, which according to Kiev are aimed at restoring a "just peace" according to the Ukrainian formula. (Text) (Text) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 Odessa (Ukraine) - The recently resumed Russian blockade of Odessa's ports accentuates the deep strangulation of the region's economy, while the city suffers for the second year in a row a blow to its status as a tourist destination. By Rostyslav Averchuk (Text) (photo) (video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 PAKISTAN ATTACK\par \par \uc2 Islamabad - The death toll in yesterday's suicide bombing during a crowded Jamiat Ulema-i-Islam (JUI-F) religious party gathering in northern Pakistan rose to 54 on Monday, with Islamic State claiming responsibility. (Text)(Photo) (Audio) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 NIGER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 Niamey - Tension after the military coup in Niger continues unabated, after the \uc2 Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS) \uc2 threatened the coup junta with the use of force if they do not release and return power within a week to the deposed president, \uc2 Mohamed Bazoum\uc2 , and France warned that it will respond if there are attacks against its nationals or companies (Text) (Text) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 Niamey - Coup plotters in Niger accuse France of wanting to "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  militarily" in the country (Text) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 Moscow - Kremlin confident that Niger will return to the "constitutional path" (SENT)\par \par \uc2 SCANDINAVIAN KORANS\par \par \uc2 Riyadh/Berlin - The \uc2 Organization of Islamic Cooperation\uc2  (\uc2 OIC\uc2 ) today demanded that the authorities in Sweden and Denmark take measures to stop the burning of copies of the Koran, a warning they have already issued in recent weeks but which has not prevented a similar incident in front of the Swedish Parliament this Monday. (Text) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 U.S. ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 Washington - Despite being imputed and facing numerous judicial fronts, former U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (2017-2021) appears unbeatable against the other Republican candidates for the primaries of his party for the elections of 2024, according to a poll published Monday by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 . (SENT)\par \par \uc2 CHINA TYPHOON\par \par \uc2 Beijing - Authorities and residents in northern China are on high alert due to the heaviest rains and storms in the last decade in the region, which left at least two dead and more than 100,000 people evacuated. (Text) (Photo) (Audio) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 LEBANON \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Beirut - The first deputy governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Lebanon\uc2 , Wissam Mansouri, took over the reins of the issuing institution on an interim basis today, marking the end of three decades of consecutive terms by the outgoing governor and corruption suspect, \uc2 Riad Salameh\uc2 . (Text) (Photo) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 - Some clues have been sent about the situation in Lebanon, a country that adds another institutional vacuum, and a profile of \uc2 Riad Salameh\uc2 . By Noem\u237\'00\'ED Jabois (Text) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 - In the same showcase of the Museum of the \uc2 Lebanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is an old banknote, in its time enough to buy a house, and the largest denomination banknote today, which is not enough for a carton of milk after the sharp devaluation suffered by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last four years. By Noem\u237\'00\'ED Jabois (Cr\u243\'00\'F3nica) (Text) (Photo) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires - Two weeks before the primary elections to define the candidates for president in Argentina, the ruling Peronism has put together a candidacy that is perceived to be competitive despite the economic crisis, which has generated such disenchantment among citizens that it is doubtful how many people will vote. (Text) (Photo) (Video) (SENT) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 ECUADOR ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 Quito - Ecuadorian presidential candidate Daniel Noboa Az\u237\'00\'EDn, running for the National Democratic Action party, assured in an interview with EFE that the country is at its most complicated moment and needs a change, which he promises to give with job creation as the main axis to solve other problems, including insecurity, which he hopes to fight with intelligence, international cooperation, modern prisons and "barge prisons". (Text) (Photo) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 PANAMA HOMOSEXUALS\par \par \uc2 Panama City - Fifteen years ago Panama decriminalized homosexuality by repealing a decree law that criminalized "sodomy", becoming the last Latin American country to do so. Shortly before, Panamanian activist Juan Alonso had been arrested for handing out condoms in a campaign against HIV. By Ana de Le\u243\'00\'F3n (Text) (Photo) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 AMAZON SUMMIT\par \par \uc2 Bel\u233\'00\'E9m (Brazil) - Bel\u233\'00\'E9m is the window chosen by Brazil to show the world the reality of the Amazon. The city is already warming up for the presidential meeting of Amazonian countries in August, which will be attended by 13 nations, including several guests, with a view to 2025, when it will host COP30. By Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Ang\u233\'00\'E9lica Troncoso (Photo)(Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 PERU PISCO\par \par \uc2 Lima - A chronological journey through 300 years of history, from 1534 to 1834, has allowed journalist \u205\'00\'CDtalo Sifuentes to offer a documented investigation to ratify the Peruvian origin of pisco and argue that his country should insist on the unanimous recognition of this appellation of origin. By David Blanco Bonilla (Text) (Video) (SENT)\par \par \uc2 NEWS AGENDA (GMT hours)\par \par \uc2 Riyadh - Scandinavian Korans - The member countries of the \uc2 Organization of Islamic Cooperation\uc2  (\uc2 OIC\uc2 ) are holding an emergency virtual meeting today at the level of foreign ministers to address the desecration of the sacred book of the Koran, following several burnings of copies in Sweden and Denmark. (Text)\par \par \uc2 2:30 p.m. - New York - U.S. Ambassador \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2  presents her monthly program of work at the Security Council, whose rotating presidency she assumes during August. (Text)\par \par \uc2 14:00h.- Moscow - RUSSIA OPPOSITION - The Russian justice system studies the appeal presented by the lawyers of the opposition leader \uc2 Vladimir Kara-Murza\uc2 , condemned to 25 years in prison for high treason, among other crimes. (Text)\par \par \uc2 11:00 a.m. - Geneva - TOBACCO HEALTH - \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO) \uc2 report on the global tobacco epidemic (Text)\par \par \uc2 PANAMA CITY - PANAMA HOMOSEXUALITY - Panama celebrates 15 years of decriminalizing homosexuality by repealing a decree law that criminalized "sodomy", becoming the last country in Latin America to do so. (Text) (Photo) (Video)\par \par \uc2 EU PHILIPPINES - The President of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , visits the Philippines, where she will meet with the Philippine President, \uc2 Ferdinand Marcos Jr\uc2 , to discuss issues such as trade, green and digital transition, as well as security. (Text) (Photo) (Video)\par \par \uc2 Beirut - LEBANON \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  - In the same showcase of the Museum of the \uc2 Lebanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is an old banknote in its time sufficient to buy a house and the largest denomination today, which is not enough for a carton of milk after the sharp devaluation suffered by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last four years. (Text) (Text)\par \par \uc2 Vatican City - POPE PORTUGAL - \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has included the stage of the Fatima Shrine in his trip to Lisbon to participate in the World Youth Day so that it becomes a moment in which he will ask for the end of all wars, especially the one in Ukraine. (Text)\par \par \uc2 16:00h.- Caracas.- VENEZUELA ELECTIONS.- The National Commission of Primaries (CNP) which governs the internal elections of the Venezuelan opposition, scheduled for October 22, informs on advances in the process of organization of these elections in which they will elect the candidate who will face Chavism in the presidential elections of 2024. (Text) (Photo) (Video)\par \par \uc2 15:00h.- Tetouan (Morocco).- MOROCCO MONARCHY.- After three years suspended due to the pandemic, King Mohamed VI presides over the ceremony known as the "beia", in which the notables pay homage to the king on the occasion of the Throne Festival, the anniversary of his enthronement. (Text) (Video)\par \par \uc2 16:00h.- New York.- UKRAINE WAR.- The \uc2 UN\uc2  humanitarian coordinator for Ukraine, Denise Brown, gives a press conference via videoconference. (Text)\par \par \uc2 12:00h.- Washington - USA BEVERAGES.- The idyll between Americans and beer is faltering, as the volume of sales has decreased in recent years, which shows a change in the consumption habits of alcoholic beverages in the country, where the options have multiplied. By Sara Soteras i Acosta (Text) (Photo)\par \par \uc2 int\par \par \uc2 Editorial staff EFE International\par \par \uc2 (34)913 46 73 03\par \par \uc2 You can write to mesacentral@efe.com to contact our editorial staff.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.efeservicios.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.efeservicios.com}}}\uc2  you will find all the multimedia production of the EFE Agency and its World Agenda, an updated list of programmed informative events.\par \par \uc2 For any other product or service, please contact clientes@efe.com or call +34 91 3467245.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230731ej7v00bi4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
