\par\par \b \uc2  Saudi riyal stable,no devaluation seen now-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tara FitzGerald \par \uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 1999\par 14:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  DUBAI, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The Saudi Arabian riyal, under the gun from slumping oil prices, is not in any immediate danger of devaluation despite reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, dealers and analysts said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "I'm not expecting any more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity for the time being...and certainly not today," one Riyadh-based dealer told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "There is no sign of devaluation on the horizon and I don't see any reason why they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would default in the near future," he added. \par \par \uc2  The kingdom, which draws around three-quarters of its revenues from oil, has seen its economy hit hard by the decline in world oil prices over the past year. \par \par \uc2  The Financial Times reported on Friday that this had resulted in a spate of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency (SAMA) or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Thursday, with pressure mounting on the riyal. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said although there had been signs of some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last week, activity had now returned to normal. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has everything under control and trading is as normal today," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The riyal normally trades in a narrow band around its peg of 3.7500 to the dollar. The dollar is the medium for pricing oil and so accounts for most Saudi exports. The kingdom is by far the world's largest oil producer and exporter. \par \par \uc2  By 1145 GMT the riyal was quoted at 3.7505/15 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  SAMA on Saturday denied reports it had been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculators. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and had no intention of changing the riyal's exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "The statement from SAMA saying that they did not see any reason why they should devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was very forthright and I firmly believe that the Saudi riyal will maintain its parity," said Badar Kazmi, regional head of treasury at Standard Chartered in Dubai. \par \par \uc2  Last August the riyal came under attack from foreign-based speculators who were betting on a devaluation as oil prices slumped. \par \par \uc2  Government sources said SAMA pumped $750 million into the market to shield the riyal on that occasion. \par \par \uc2  The Saudi government traditionally defends its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than by increasing interest rates. \b \highlight22\uc2 Saudi Arabia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1986. \par \par \uc2  Diplomats in Riyadh have estimated that the Saudi government would spend up to $20 billion defending the riyal if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether he envisaged any more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near future, Kazmi said some activity was always part of a regular monetary and exchange policy. \par \par \uc2  "They will come in enough to ward off any attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which as a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  they should be doing," Kazmi said. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to see these blips here and there, but there really doesn't seem to be any major fault in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as such." \par \par \uc2  The Saudi newspaper al-Eqtisadiah said the Saudi Arabian stock market also felt the weight of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with its fall of 13.41 points or one percent to 1331.01 by Saturday's close mainly caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2s03ply\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
